<body>
<div class="container mt-5 mb-5" style="max-width:760px">
  <h1 class="mb-3">Partner API</h1>
  <p><a href="/">&larr; Back to Larkmoor</a></p>

  <p>Larkmoor's Partner API authenticates B2B integrations using a signed JWT assertion in the
    <code>Authorization</code> header, instead of a shared password. Each request must carry:</p>
  <pre class="bg-light p-3"><code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;assertion JWT&gt;</code></pre>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Signing your assertion</h2>
  <p>Assertions are RS256-signed JSON Web Tokens. Partners sign their assertion with an RSA
    private key and may include their certificate directly in the token via the
    <code>x5c</code> header for convenience, so our verifier can validate the signature without a
    separate key-exchange step ahead of time.</p>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Endpoints</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>POST /partner-api/sync-customers</code> &mdash; returns the customer records your
      account is entitled to, scoped by the <code>partner_id</code> claim in your assertion.</li>
    <li><code>POST /partner-api/legacy/refund</code> &mdash; our older refund integration,
      predating the certificate-based flow above. It authenticates with an HS256 assertion
      referencing a partner's registered signing key by name via the <code>kid</code> header.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Claims</h2>
  <p>Every assertion must carry a <code>partner_id</code> claim identifying your account. See
    <a href="/partners">our partners</a> for examples of registered partner IDs.</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>
